nconsistency: after this item, all stacks read from a single authoritative table\\n- Provides a citable Source ID system enabling benchmark evals (#2251) to assert on Source field values\\n- Reduces duplication: false-positive guards unified in one `## What Not To Flag` section\\n- Enables the Health Score (#2253) to reference a single severity tier table\\n- Provides `agents/code-reviewer.md` Step 6 a definitive load instruction\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `agents/code-reviewer.md` begins a review, it loads `dh:code-review-shared` before loading any per-stack skill. The shared skill provides: (1) the four-part Iron Law finding format, (2) the Critical/Warning/Suggestion severity tier table with deduction values, (3) the canonical report markdown template, (4) false-positive guard rules that apply across all stacks, (5) a source registry at `references/source-registry.md` listing every named principle. Each per-stack `SKILL.md` opens with `Load /dh:code-review-shared first.` and references Source IDs from the registry in its rules.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n```text\\nplugins/development-harness/skills/code-review-shared/\\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 SKILL.md                    # Iron Law, severity tiers, report template, What Not To Flag\\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 references/\\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 source-registry.md      # Book/principle coverage matrix with Source IDs\\n```\\n\\nAll 8 per-stack SKILL.md files each contain `Load /dh:code-review-shared first.` as their opening instruction.\\n\\n`agents/code-reviewer.md` Step 6 reads: `Load dh:code-review-shared first, then load the matching dh:code-review-{stack} skill.`\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `ls plugins/development-harness/skills/code-review-shared/` returns `SKILL.md` and `references/`\\n2. `ls plugins/development-harness/skills/code-review-shared/references/` returns `source-registry.md`\\n3. `code-review-shared/SKILL.md` contains sections: Iron Law (four-part format), Severity Tiers (Critical/Warning/Suggestion table), Report Template, What Not To Flag\\n4. `grep -l 'Load /dh:code-review-shared' plugins/development-harness/skills/code-review-*/SKILL.md` returns one line per code-review skill (8 files)\\n5. `agents/code-reviewer.md` Step 6 instruction references loading `code-review-shared` before the per-stack skill\\n6. `source-registry.md` contains at least one Source ID entry per per-stack skill domain (Python, TypeScript, Node.js, Web, CLI, LLM, Claude Skills, Architecture)\\n7. `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/development-harness/skills/code-review-shared/SKILL.md` exits 0\\n8. Frontmatter includes `user-invocable: false`\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/code-review-python/SKILL.md` \u2014 example per-stack skill structure and frontmatter |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md` \u2014 Step 3 stack detection table, Step 6 apply rules, Step 8 report assembly |\\n| Research | `research/coding-agents/brooks-lint.md` \u2014 Iron Law definition, severity tiers, `_shared/` directory pattern |\\n| Research | `research/insights/2026-05-10-brooks-lint-improvements.md` \u2014 Improvement 2 (code-review-shared) target state detail |\\n| Constraint | `.claude/CLAUDE.md` subdirectory namespacing rule \u2014 skills must be one level deep under `skills/` |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 this is the foundational item\\n- Blocks: #2248 (Iron Law structured diagnosis chain), #2251 (eval/benchmark suite), #2253 (Health Score)\\n- Related (parallel-safe): #2252 (auto-scope detection) \u2014 does not depend on shared skill content\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 creating one new skill directory with SKILL.md and one references file, then updating 8 existing SKILL.md files with a single-line load instruction and Source ID annotations. Research (brooks-lint) provides exact content for Iron Law, severity tiers, and shared template. Main e