constraint, skill directory depth rule (one level under `skills/`), and frontmatter convention are all AVAILABLE and verified \u2014 no alignment risk from structural constraints.\\n\\n**Conclusion**: ALIGNMENT_CLEAN. Implementation can proceed from design intent without remediation.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md` Step 6 \u2014 currently references only per-stack skill loading; must add `Load dh:code-review-shared first` instruction\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated to new interface\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated (`agents/code-reviewer.md` Step 6)\\n- [ ] Every agent instruction updated (8 per-stack SKILL.md files)\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated or removed (N/A \u2014 additive change)\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated (N/A \u2014 CI uses external plugin unaffected)\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n**SDLC layer blast radius** (verified 2026-05-29):\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n\\n**Rationale**: The code-review skill system permits agents to load per-stack skills without a canonical shared definition of severity tiers, Iron Law format, or false-positive guards. Each per-stack skill independently restates these dimensions \u2014 a gate that should enforce a common standard (the shared skill) does not exist yet. This is not a defect (no traceable failure chain), not a recurring pattern (first occurrence of this gap being addressed), and not a typo/surface fix. It fits missing-guardrail: the system allowed per-stack inconsistency because no mechanism prevented it.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: design-framing (unbounded-design path is appropriate since this is a new capability; however missing-guardrail classification is more precise given the specific gap)\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: `agents/code-reviewer.md` loads per-stack skills without a shared baseline \u2192 inconsistent severity judgments, undefined Iron Law format, no common false-positive guards \u2192 `code-review-shared` loaded before per-stack skills enforces the shared baseline\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING**\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: feat: code-review: Add code-review-shared skill with Iron Law, severity tiers, report template, and source registry\\nDate: 2026-05-29\\nGoal: Create a foundational shared code-review skill that standardizes Iron Law format, severity tiers, report template, and false-positive guards across all 8 per-stack code-review skills.\\n\\nConditions:\\n\\n| Input | Status | Citation |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Item description: Iron Law, severity tiers, report template, false-positive guards, source registry |\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | Directory listing 2026-05-29: 8 skills confirmed (code-review-python, typescript, nodejs, web, cli, llm, claude-skills, architecture); `code-review-shared` confirmed absent |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | `code-review-python/SKILL.md` frontmatter confirms `user-invocable: false` convention; brooks-lint research file confirms `_shared/` pattern |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | `grep -rn code-review-shared plugins/development-harness/` returns empty \u2014 no shared baseline exists |\\n| Constraints | AVAILABLE | `.claude/CLAUDE.md` confirms skills must be one level under `skills/`; `user-invocable: false` confirmed |\\n| Verification expectations | AVAILABLE | Measurable signal provides exact bash commands; all Fact-Check claims VERIFIED |\\n| Iron Law content | AVAILABLE | `research/coding-agents/brooks-lint.md` line 64: four-part format Symptom \u2192 Source \u2192 Consequence \u2192 Remedy |\\n| Severity tier content | AVAILABLE | `research/coding-agents/brooks-lint.md` lines 140\u2013143: Critical \u221215, Warning \u22125, Suggestion \u22121 |\\n| Affected file count | AVAILABLE | Directory listing confirms 8 per-stack SKILL.md files (not 7 \u2014 code-review-architecture included) |\\n| Downstream items | AVAILABLE | #2248, #2251, #2253 confirmed as dependent in backlog |\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 10\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\n\\nChanges from initial snapshot:\\n- Affected file count: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by directory listing: 8 skills confirmed, not 7)\\n- All other conditions: AVAILABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (no degradation)\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n\\n**Blocking items**: None. All inputs are AVAILABLE. Ready for SAM planning.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n**Feature Gap Reproducibility** (verified 2026-05-29):\\n\\nThis is a feature request, not a defect. \\\"Reproducibility\\\" applies to the observable evidence of the gap.\\n\\n**Observable gap \u2014 run these commands to confirm the current state:**\\n\\n```bash\\n# Confirm code-review-shared skill does NOT exist\\nls plugins/development-harness/skills/ | grep code-review-shared\\n# Expected output: (empty \u2014 directory does not exist)\\n\\n# Confirm 8 per-stack skills exist without shared load instruction\\ngrep -l \\\"Load /dh:code-review-shared\\\" plugins/development-harness/skills/code-review-*/SKILL.md\\n# Expected output: (empty \u2014 no file contains this instruction)\\n\\n# Confirm agents/code-reviewer.md Step 6 has no shared skill load\\ngrep \\\"code-review-shared\\\\|Iron Law\\\" plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md\\n# Expected output: (empty \u2014 neither term appears)\\n```\\n\\n**Environment**: All commands run from `/home/user/claude_skills` (repo root). No setup required \u2014 gap is observable via file system.\\n\\n**Completion signal (post-implementation):**\\n```bash\\nls plugins/development-harness/skills/code-review-shared/\\n# Expected: SKILL.md  references/\\n\\ngrep -l \\\"Load /dh:code-review-shared\\\" plugins/development-harness/skills/code-review-*/SKILL.md | wc -l\\n# Expected: 8\\n\\ngrep \\\"code-review-shared\\\" plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md\\n# Expected: one or more lines containing the load instruction\\n```\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n| System | Role | Connection |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `code-review-shared/SKILL.md` (new) | Defines shared Iron Law, severity tiers, report template | Loaded first by code-reviewer agent before any per-stack skill |\\n| `code-review-shared/references/source-registry.md` (new) | Source ID registry | Referenced from findings in per-stack SKILL.md files |\\n| `code-review-{python,typescript,nodejs,web,cli,llm,claude-skills,architecture}/SKILL.md` (8 existing) | Per-stack rules | Each gains `Load /dh:code-review-shared first.` opening line |\\n| `agents/code-reviewer.md` | Orchestrates the review workflow | Step 6 updated to load shared skill before per-stack |\\n| `skills/forensic-review/SKILL.md` | SAM S6 stage | Dispatches code-reviewer agent \u2014 inherits shared severity table transitively |\\n| Items #2248, #2251, #2253 | Downstream backlog items | All depend on severity tiers and source registry defined here |\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe seven local code-review skills (`code-review-python`, `code-review-typescript`, `code-review-nodejs`, `code-review-web`, `code-review-cli`, `code-review-llm`, `code-review-claude-skills`) each contain a single `SKILL.md` with stack-specific rules:\\n\\n```bash\\nls plugins/development-harness/skills/code-review-*/\\n# returns only SKILL.md for each\\n```\\n\\nThere is no shared file defining:\\n\\n- The severity tier table (Critical / Warning / Suggestion) \u2014 currently inferred per-stack\\n- The standard report template \u2014 defined inline in `agents/code-reviewer.md` Output Format only, not loaded by skills\\n- The \\\"what not to flag\\\" guards (false-positive avoidance discipline)\\n- A book/principle coverage matrix that the cited Source field draws from\\n\\nEach stack skill restates the patterns differently. There is no `code-review-shared` skill or `_shared/` directory under `skills/` that the per-stack skills can reference. This is the gap that brooks-lint's `skills/_shared/` (common.md, decay-risks.md, source-coverage.md, remedy-guide.md) closes \u2014 README.md lines 388\u2013396, CLAUDE.md lines 18\u201319, 27\u201332.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new skill `plugins/development-harness/skills/code-review-shared/SKILL.md` exists. It contains:\\n\\n- **Iron Law** \u2014 the four-part Symptom/Source/Consequence/Remedy format\\n- **Severity tiers** \u2014 table mapping severity labels (Critical/Warning/Suggestion) to deductions and PR-block behaviour\\n- **Report template** \u2014 the canonical markdown structure for a `codebase-analysis` artifact\\n- **What Not To Flag** \u2014 guards against common false-positive patterns\\n- **Source registry** \u2014 a `references/source-registry.md` listing every named principle that any rule cites (named after `source-coverage.md` in brooks-lint)\\n\\nEach `code-review-{stack}` SKILL.md begins with: `Load /dh:code-review-shared first.` Each stack-specific rule is rewritten to reference a Source ID from the registry.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n```bash\\nls plugins/development-harness/skills/code-review-shared/\\n# returns: SKILL.md, references/\\n\\nls plugins/development-harness/skills/code-review-shared/references/\\n# returns: source-registry.md (and other shared references)\\n\\ngrep -l \\\"Load /dh:code-review-shared\\\" plugins/development-harness/skills/code-review-*/SKILL.md\\n# returns one line per stack-specific code-review skill\\n```\\n\\nThe `agents/code-reviewer.md` Step 6 (\\\"Apply Stack-Specific Rules\\\") instruction is updated to load `code-review-shared` first, then the matching `code-review-{stack}`.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"6e776eebc14a05cccf75f41456b0d96bea8d919ded37659807063f2d6650db25\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg28Vw\"}"}